# Suite memmap: profile-driven memory system through its bus function (plan 03-04).
# Fixed cases, then memmap.anchor.<region>-lo|hi for every region row of the test, then the
# literal-map family (plan 03-06): the decode dump against the literal map, one case per row of
# data/memmap/intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1.literal.txt (memmap.row.<view>-<LO>-<HI>), and one case
# per gate of the literal (memmap.row-gate.<gate>-closed).
# Plan 05-04: the PSG region is a real device; memmap.width.psg8-low-byte-upper-zero is new and the rows R and W 01F0-01FF are split by register width (the shape register and the two ports are declared exception rows of the literal).
# Plan 06-06 (A-01, D-04): the five STIC regions are the real device stic14; the STIC rows of the literal are split by register width (new row ids), memmap.width.stub-reads-ffff became memmap.width.stic14-registers and memmap.describe.stub-vs-undriven became memmap.describe.stic-vs-undriven.
